# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Credentials and account state — NEVER commit.
# Paths are configurable (KIRO_CREDS_FILE, ACCOUNTS_CONFIG_FILE,
# ACCOUNTS_STATE_FILE in conduit/config.py).
#
# credentials.json and state.json are the ACTUAL config.py defaults for
# ACCOUNTS_CONFIG_FILE / ACCOUNTS_STATE_FILE, and were missing here: an earlier
# version of this comment claimed the patterns below were "the defaults" while
# listing neither. They are the files an operator really creates — the app's
# startup handler loads exactly those names — so `git add .` would have staged
# live cloud credentials. Keep this list in sync with config.py.
credentials.json
state.json
kiro-creds*.json
accounts.json
accounts_state.json
*.credentials.json

# Local state / debug output (KIRO_CLI_DB_FILE, DEBUG_DIR)
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
debug/

# Tooling
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
